---
/**
 * A user-state page. Everything on it comes out of the reader's own browser and
 * none of it exists at build time, so it carries noindex, is excluded from the
 * sitemap, and is deliberately NOT disallowed in robots.txt — a blocked path is
 * never fetched, so the tag would never be read.
 *
 * `client:only` for the same reason: rendering an empty shelf on the server and
 * replacing it a moment later is a layout shift for markup nobody reads.
 */
import MyBar from '../components/bar/MyBar.svelte';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="My Bar — eXir" description="Tell eXir what is on your shelf and it will tell you what you can make." noindex current="my-bar">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>My Bar</h1>
    <p class="lede">What you can make from what you already have, and which single bottle would unlock the most.</p>
  </section>

  {/* The island renders nothing until it hydrates, so its slot is zero-high
      and everything below it — the footer, the explanatory prose — starts at
      the top of the page and drops into place a moment later. That is a
      layout shift of almost half a viewport, measured, and it is the cost of
      `client:only` rather than an argument against it: none of this page is
      true at build time, so there is nothing honest to server-render.

      The space is reserved instead, the same way the navigation count reserves
      two digits before it knows the number. The placeholder is real markup so
      the area is not blank while the module arrives, and the island removes it
      on mount. */}
  <div class="tool-shell">
    <p class="wrap aside" data-tool-placeholder>Reading your shelf…</p>
    <MyBar client:only="svelte" />
  </div>

  <div class="wrap notes">
    <div class="card glass note-card">
      <h2 class="card-title">What this remembers</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this page leaves your browser. There are no accounts here and nothing to sign
        in to, which also means what you save lives in one browser on one device and the site
        cannot move it for you.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card glass note-card">
      <h2 class="card-title">What is not counted</h2>
      <p>
        Pantry staples — sugar, water, salt, a lemon — are assumed rather than matched, so they
        are not on the list above and never count against a drink. Garnishes never block a match
        either: nobody is stopped from making a Negroni by having no orange.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
